    "data": {
      "text": "Vaibhav S/O Bhaskar Bhoyar And 2 Others vs The State Of Mah. \nThr. Pso, Nagbhid Ps, ... on 12 February, 2024\nAuthor: Vinay Joshi\nBench: Vinay Joshi\nOrder \n 1\n In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay\n Nagpur Bench, Nagpur. \n Criminal Application [Apl] No. 199/2024. \n Vaibhav Bhaskar Bhoyar and others. \n -Versus-\n State of Maharashtra\nOffice notes, Office Memoranda of\nCoram, appearances, Court's orders Court's or Judge's Orders\nor directions and Registrar's orders. \n Shri S.A. Mohta, Advocate for Applicants. \n Shri M. Badar, A.P.P. for the Non-applicant. \n Coram : Vinay Joshi And\n Vrushali V. Joshi, Jj. \n Date : February 12, 2024. \n Heard. \n2.  This is an application seeking to quash charge-sheet bearing S.C.C.No.844/2023 arising out of first information report bearing Crime No.99/2023 registered with Nagbhid Police Station, District Chandrapur for the offence punishable under Sections 273, 188 of the Indian Penal Code and Section 59[i] of the Food Safety and Standards Act. \n3. The learned Counsel for applicants would submit that applicants are also gratuitous Rgd. \nOrder 1202apl199.24 passenger having no concern with the seizure. Our attention has been invited to the orders passed by this Court in Criminal Application No.198/2024 dated 06.02.2024, where in Vaibhav S/O Bhaskar Bhoyar And 2 Others vs The State Of Mah. Thr. Pso, Nagbhid Ps, ... on 12 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97240408/\n1 similar circumstances interim relief has been granted.\n4. Issue notice to non-applicants, returnable on 19.03.2024. Learned A.P.P. waives notice for the non-applicant. \n5. The trial Court shall not proceed further with the matter till the returnable date. \nJUDGE JUDGE Signed by: R.G. Dhuriya (RGD) Designation: PS To Honourable Judge Date:\n13/02/2024 11:24:57 Rgd.\nVaibhav S/O Bhaskar Bhoyar And 2 Others vs The State Of Mah. Thr. Pso, Nagbhid Ps, ... on 12 February, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97240408/\n2",
